<p>Louisville is a logistics town with a party calendar. UPS runs its global air hub at the airport, Ford builds trucks at two plants, and Humana, Norton Healthcare and GE Appliances employ tens of thousands. Then every spring the Kentucky Derby Festival turns the whole city into a two-week event. That mix is why the best side hustles in Louisville lean practical: driving, cleaning, hosting, sorting packages and fixing up old houses, timed to the moments when demand spikes.</p>
<p>Below are 18 side gigs that work here right now, with typical pay, startup costs and the local details that matter. We also cover the Louisville Metro occupational license tax, which catches a lot of new side hustlers off guard.</p>

