<h2 id="why-louisville">What makes Louisville good for side gigs</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Derby season is a money machine.</strong> Thunder Over Louisville kicks off the festival in April, the Oaks and Derby run the first weekend in May, and hotel rooms, rentals, rides and staff are in short supply the whole time.</li>
  <li><strong>The fall festival run.</strong> The Kentucky State Fair in August, Bourbon &amp; Beyond and Louder Than Life in September, and the St. James Court Art Show in Old Louisville each October bring a second wave of visitors.</li>
  <li><strong>Bourbon tourism.</strong> Distilleries along Whiskey Row and the Urban Bourbon Trail keep visitors flowing year-round, which supports rideshare, rentals and hospitality work.</li>
  <li><strong>Low costs.</strong> Rent and home prices sit well below most metros, so remote income and weekend gigs go further than they would in Nashville or Chicago.</li>
</ul>

