    <p>Work the airport (Louisville Muhammad Ali International), weekend nights on Bardstown Road and in NuLu, Cardinals games and concerts at the KFC Yum! Center, and every day of Derby week. Bourbon tourists who don't want to drive between downtown distilleries are steady fares. Start with our <a href="/lyft-uber/">Lyft and Uber guide</a>.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $15–$26/hr before gas and wear</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Eligible car, insurance</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Event weekends and nights</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="delivery">2. Food and grocery delivery</h3>
    <p>DoorDash, Uber Eats, Grubhub and Instacart all run busy here. St. Matthews, the Highlands and the Oxmoor area pack restaurants close together, while Prospect and Anchorage tip well on grocery orders. Rainy spring evenings pay best.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $14–$22/hr before gas</li><li><b>Startup:</b> Car or e-bike, [[amazon:insulated-bag|insulated delivery bag]]</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Flexible evenings</li></ul>
